ckle cell anemia</article-title><source>West Afr J Med</source><year>1996</year><volume>15</volume><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9020595</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B8"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Hilton</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Osborn</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Knight</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Singhal</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Serjeant</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Psychiatric complications of homozygous sickle cell disease among young adults in the Jamaican Cohort study</article-title><source>Br J Psychiatry</source><year>1997</year><volume>170</volume><fpage>67</fpage><lpage>76</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1192/bjp.170.1.69</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B9"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Iloeje</surname><given-names>SO</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Psychiatric morbidity among children with sickle &#x02013; cell disease</article-title><source>Dev Med Child Neurol</source><year>1991</year><volume>33</volume><fpage>1087</fpage><lpage>94</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">1778345</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B10"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><collab>W.H.O.</collab></person-group><article-title>International Classification of Diseases, (ICD- 10)</article-title><source>World Health Organization (WHO)</source><year>1992</year><edition>10</edition></citation></ref><ref id="B11"><citation citation-type="book"><article-title>Diagnostic and Statistical Manual of Mental Disorders, (DSM- IV)</article-title><source>American Psychiatric Association</source><year>1994</year><edition>4</edition></citation></ref><ref id="B12"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><sur